  "$description": "Type composites — CANON (promoted 2026-07-17 from tokens/_proposals/typography-composites-2026-07-17.json). Apollo SDS role layer over the primitives in typography.json. TWO sets: Editorial (full line-height) + Component (cap-trim, seated in a 4px grid-slot). BRAND RULE: no light/ultra on body sizes (font-5/6/7 min regular; no dark step-up there). -V2 dark step-up applies to display+heading only. Rendered CSS: knowledge/canon/type.css. Not wired into gen_canon_tokens (consumed via the type.css composite classes, not as flat vars). — DTCG RE-ENCODE (s141, enacts s136-D1 axis A wire-format clause): each composite is now a W3C DTCG $type:\"typography\" token. $value carries the DTCG sub-values (fontFamily/fontSize/fontWeight/letterSpacing/lineHeight); every Apollo-specific field (the default/emphasis weight pair, weight-dark, trim, slot, descender-guard) is PRESERVED VERBATIM under $extensions[\"com.apollo.sds\"]. Nothing was dropped. OPEN ($doubt, s141): the Component set carries no lineHeight — it is seated by cap-trim into a 4px slot — and strict DTCG requires the key; supplying one is a design decision, so the key is OMITTED pending Dave's ruling rather than invented.",
